###    result
起初<09002><07225>，　神<0430>創造<1254>{<0853>}天<8064>{<0853>}地<0776>。

Placement rationale (brief, not part of the output line):
- 起初 ← בְּרֵאשִׁית: carries both the inseparable prefix בְּ `<09002>` ("in") and רֵאשִׁית `<7225>` ("beginning").
- 神 ← אֱלֹהִים `<0430>`; 創造 ← בָּרָא `<1254>` (Chinese God-created order matches).
- {<0853>}天 / {<0853>}地 ← the two אֵת object markers (no Chinese word → braced) attached to הַשָּׁמַיִם `<8064>` and הָאָרֶץ `<0776>`.
- The article הַ `<09009>` and the conjunction וְ are **not** emitted: Chinese 天地 expresses no definiteness or explicit "and", so those morphemes have no UNV surface position. Only the בְּ prefix is expressed (via 起初).




